WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.159 --> 00:00:01.365
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.365 --> 00:00:02.819
Today's message is-

00:00:02.819 --> 00:00:04.596
- Turn pain into greatness.

00:00:04.596 --> 00:00:06.629
Over to you, Machine Gun Kelly.

00:00:06.629 --> 00:00:08.589
(rooster crows)

00:00:08.589 --> 00:00:11.420
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.155
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:14.155 --> 00:00:18.366
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.366 --> 00:00:20.637
- People used to take my
raps and crunch 'em up

00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:21.992
and throw 'em on the ground.

00:00:21.992 --> 00:00:23.422
I used to get made fun of all the time

00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:25.525
'cause who believes that the guy sittin'

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.087
next to 'em in math
class is going to blow up

00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:27.920
and become a superstar?

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.503
You don't believe that, right?

00:00:29.503 --> 00:00:32.063
But you should have and it's a bummer.

00:00:32.063 --> 00:00:34.447
'Cause, I don't know, man.

00:00:34.447 --> 00:00:38.237
I mean take it and pain
is the best inspiration.

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:40.025
So if you're a creative out there

00:00:40.025 --> 00:00:40.858
and you're getting bullied,

00:00:40.858 --> 00:00:42.430
take it and make
something great out of it.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:43.785
- So what do you think?

00:00:43.785 --> 00:00:45.798
- I think that' a really
important message.

00:00:45.798 --> 00:00:48.669
When I first started dancing,

00:00:48.669 --> 00:00:53.229
I was told that I would be
a decent dancer, at best.

00:00:53.229 --> 00:00:54.513
- At best?

00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:56.029
- At best, at best.

00:00:56.029 --> 00:00:58.816
I wasn't very good and
my feet are actually

00:00:58.816 --> 00:01:03.000
not equipped to dance because
I have really flat feet

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.004
and I used to get a lot of pain in my feet

00:01:06.004 --> 00:01:09.779
and it would always shake,
especially during performances.

00:01:09.779 --> 00:01:12.078
I told myself that I'm
going to make myself strong.

00:01:12.078 --> 00:01:15.929
So I did really, really
painful ballet exercises

00:01:15.929 --> 00:01:18.454
and eventually I became stronger

00:01:18.454 --> 00:01:21.866
and now I'm able to go
on stage and perform

00:01:21.866 --> 00:01:25.366
and also change the physiology of my foot.

00:01:26.866 --> 00:01:29.254
I wish I could show you
but I can't right now.

00:01:29.254 --> 00:01:31.266
But I never had an arch
but I have an arch now.

00:01:31.266 --> 00:01:32.099
- Wow.

00:01:32.099 --> 00:01:34.579
- Yes and to most people
it's not a big deal

00:01:34.579 --> 00:01:36.841
but to me is a huge
deal because I was told

00:01:36.841 --> 00:01:39.066
I couldn't be a dancer because of my feet.

00:01:39.066 --> 00:01:39.899
- Cool.

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:44.104
When I was at my agency, when
I first connected with them,

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:46.804
they told me that I wasn't
good enough to join the agency.

00:01:46.804 --> 00:01:48.591
They liked my message but
I couldn't speak which hurt

00:01:48.591 --> 00:01:51.504
because I'd already done
two years of public speaking

00:01:51.504 --> 00:01:54.704
and I felt like I should
be a little better

00:01:54.704 --> 00:01:56.077
than I can't speak.

00:01:56.077 --> 00:01:57.991
Most of the people at their agency,

00:01:57.991 --> 00:02:01.604
they said could speak but
they didn't have a message.

00:02:01.604 --> 00:02:03.891
So they were willing to take a risk on me.

00:02:03.891 --> 00:02:05.764
I worked really hard.

00:02:05.764 --> 00:02:07.757
I wanted to take that pain, that rejection

00:02:07.757 --> 00:02:09.693
and turn it into something amazing.

00:02:09.693 --> 00:02:11.485
So I practice every single day,

00:02:11.485 --> 00:02:14.108
working on my creation story.

00:02:14.108 --> 00:02:16.575
Sometimes three times a day
making videos back and forth

00:02:16.575 --> 00:02:17.739
and back and forth.

00:02:17.739 --> 00:02:18.863
And I started getting better.

00:02:18.863 --> 00:02:21.002
In a couple months I
became the best practiced

00:02:21.002 --> 00:02:23.302
at the agency and people were saying

00:02:23.302 --> 00:02:24.766
you should go look at what Evan's doing.

00:02:24.766 --> 00:02:25.899
Not because I was great.

00:02:25.899 --> 00:02:27.662
I had the least talent of anybody there.

00:02:27.662 --> 00:02:28.820
I just worked hard.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:30.438
I was making three videos a day

00:02:30.438 --> 00:02:32.236
where most people were
having a hard time coming up

00:02:32.236 --> 00:02:33.942
with one video a week, coming with excuses

00:02:33.942 --> 00:02:36.389
that say I don't have time
to make one video a week.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.850
More than that is just too much.

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.329
That's why I got better.

00:02:39.329 --> 00:02:41.219
If you have a goal or
somebody's telling you

00:02:41.219 --> 00:02:43.029
that you can't do it, it's just work.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.838
Put in the work, get better at it.

00:02:44.838 --> 00:02:46.273
Practice, practice, practice.

00:02:46.273 --> 00:02:47.783
You can become a better speaker.

00:02:47.783 --> 00:02:49.844
You can change the physiology of your foot

00:02:49.844 --> 00:02:51.096
and become a great dancer.

00:02:51.096 --> 00:02:52.740
Whatever your goal is you can chase it

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:54.457
if you put in the work.

00:02:54.457 --> 00:02:56.489
The question of the day today is:

00:02:56.489 --> 00:02:57.866
- What is the pain that you're struggling

00:02:57.866 --> 00:03:00.015
with right now to overcome?

00:03:00.015 --> 00:03:00.848
- I love it.

00:03:00.848 --> 00:03:01.681
Leave it in the comments.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:02.676
We'll join in the discussion.

00:03:02.676 --> 00:03:04.522
Finally, want to give
a quick shout to Ron.

00:03:04.522 --> 00:03:05.865
Ron, thank you so much for picking up

00:03:05.865 --> 00:03:07.771
a copy of my book: Your One Word.

00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:09.552
It really, really means a lot me

00:03:09.552 --> 00:03:11.494
and I hope you're enjoying the reading.

00:03:11.494 --> 00:03:12.908
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:03:12.908 --> 00:03:14.070
We believe in you.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:16.499
We hope you continue
to believe in yourself

00:03:16.499 --> 00:03:19.201
and whatever your one word is much love

00:03:19.201 --> 00:03:21.405
and we'll see you again
tomorrow morning for another

00:03:21.405 --> 00:03:22.717
- Shot of espresso.

00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:25.217
♫ I wake up every morning

00:03:25.217 --> 00:03:29.278
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:03:29.278 --> 00:03:31.501
(keyboard typing)

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:34.409
- One does have to be
focused on the short term

00:03:34.409 --> 00:03:36.045
and money coming in
when creating a company

00:03:36.045 --> 00:03:40.004
because otherwise the company will die.

00:03:40.004 --> 00:03:43.004
A lot of times people think creating

00:03:43.931 --> 00:03:46.420
a company is going to be fun.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.253
I would say it's really not that fun.

00:03:48.253 --> 00:03:49.580
I mean there are periods of fun

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:53.784
and there are periods
where it's just awful.

00:03:53.784 --> 00:03:57.187
Particularly, if you're a CEO of a company

00:03:57.187 --> 00:03:58.625
you actually have a distillation

00:03:58.625 --> 00:04:01.187
of all the worst problems in the company.

00:04:01.187 --> 00:04:03.600
There's no point in spending your time

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.554
on things that are going right.

00:04:05.554 --> 00:04:07.509
You're only spending your time on things

00:04:07.509 --> 00:04:09.068
that are going wrong.

00:04:09.068 --> 00:04:10.440
There are things that are going wrong

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:12.766
that other people can't take care of.

00:04:12.766 --> 00:04:14.386
So you have the worst.

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:17.111
You have a filter for the
crappest problems in the company.

00:04:17.111 --> 00:04:21.278
(laughs) The most pernicious
and painful problem.

00:04:22.635 --> 00:04:26.718
I think you have to feel
quite compelled to do it

00:04:27.811 --> 00:04:30.113
and have a fairly high pain threshold.

00:04:30.113 --> 00:04:31.892
There's a friend of mine who says

00:04:31.892 --> 00:04:33.690
starting a company is like staring

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.357
into the abyss and eating glass.

00:04:37.279 --> 00:04:39.862
And there's some truth to that.

00:04:41.297 --> 00:04:42.713
The staring into the abyss part is

00:04:42.713 --> 00:04:44.326
that you're going to be constantly facing

00:04:44.326 --> 00:04:47.076
the extermination of the company.

00:04:48.279 --> 00:04:50.689
Because most start-ups fail.

00:04:50.689 --> 00:04:52.123
It's like 90%.

00:04:52.123 --> 00:04:55.373
It could be 99% of start-ups fail.

00:04:56.285 --> 00:04:58.937
That's the staring into the abyss part.

00:04:58.937 --> 00:05:00.085
You're constantly saying, okay,

00:05:00.085 --> 00:05:04.530
if I don't get this right
the company will die

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.947
which can be quite stressful.

00:05:08.013 --> 00:05:12.013
Then the eating glass
part is you've got to work

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.996
on the problems that the
company needs you to work on

00:05:16.996 --> 00:05:19.475
and not the problems you want to work on.

00:05:19.475 --> 00:05:22.450
So you end up working on problems

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:26.610
that you really wish
you weren't working on.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:29.027
That's the eating glass part.

00:05:29.978 --> 00:05:31.484
And that goes on for a long time.

